;;; ======================================================================
;;; (7) THE DERIVATIVES: cos' = -sin, sin' = cos on CC.  From (35) and exp' = exp:
;;; x |-> c x has derivative c (a quadratic bound with M = 0), x |-> exp(c x) has
;;; derivative c exp(c x) (chain rule), a constant multiple multiplies the
;;; derivative (product with a constant), and a sum adds them; then cos and sin
;;; are a exp(ix) + b exp(-ix) with (a, b) = (1/2, 1/2) and (1/(2i), -1/(2i)).
;;; (The notes differentiate the series termwise; the route through (35) needs
;;; no second application of 2.10.)
;;; ======================================================================
